WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.103
Week 22: Double Pronouns, Se, and Reference. report accidental events give concise instructions maintain reference across sentences

2
00:00:09.103 --> 00:00:30.759
Read for the situation. A Julia se le borró un archivo importante. Se lo comunicó al equipo, recuperaron una copia y documentaron la solución para que no volviera a ocurrir. Julia accidentally deleted an important file. She reported it to the team, they recovered a copy, and they documented the solution so that it would not happen again.

3
00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:39.329
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:45.019
Reading activities. Reading activity 52; Reading activity 53

5
00:00:45.019 --> 00:00:52.799
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:52.799 --> 00:01:18.545
Model language. Se me perdieron las llaves. — I lost my keys. El informe se lo mandé a Clara. — I sent the report to Clara. A ellos se les olvidó la cita. — They forgot the appointment. Explícaselo antes de la reunión. — Explain it to him or her before the meeting. No se nos cayó el equipo; falló el soporte. — We did not drop the equipment; the support failed.

7
00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:28.294
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
